    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23251" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inflexus</span></b> , ūs, m.
		inflecto, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a bending</i>, <i>curving</i>, <i>inflecting</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vicorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					3, 237</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adire inflexibus flexuosis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 57</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vocem inflexu modulationis torquere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Brev. Vit. 12, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
